[
    {
        "content": "<p>Can someone remark on how the new SAIR competition relates to the existing kernel arena? <a href=\"https://competition.sair.foundation/competitions/lean-kernel-challenge/overview\">https://competition.sair.foundation/competitions/lean-kernel-challenge/overview</a></p>",
        "id": 619117066,
        "sender_full_name": "Yakov Pechersky",
        "timestamp": 1787687938
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Unrelated. In the Kernel Arena, Kernels compete. In the SAIR competition, proofs compete</p>",
        "id": 619117242,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1787687984
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"470149\">Joachim Breitner</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Lean.20Kernel.20Arena/near/619117242\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Unrelated. In the Kernel Arena, Kernels compete. In the SAIR competition, proofs compete</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>What does it mean for proofs to compete? The competition description page is very vague.</p>",
        "id": 623888146,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1789318210
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The  arena compares kernels,  SAIR compares proof-carrying optimizations to the kernel.. So the proof isn’t really competing on its own- the verified improvement is</p>",
        "id": 623888860,
        "sender_full_name": "Heath Sanchez ☉",
        "timestamp": 1789318750
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What is a proof-carrying optimisation?</p>",
        "id": 623888918,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1789318796
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Like, are you given a proof, and being asked to golf it or optimise the proof so that the proof typechecks faster?</p>",
        "id": 623888990,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1789318829
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Not proof-golfing.. correct me if I’m wrong Joachim but my read is that the computation/implementation is what you optimise.. the proof certifies that the optimisation is correct. I think they are still discussing the  exact submission unit</p>",
        "id": 623889264,
        "sender_full_name": "Heath Sanchez ☉",
        "timestamp": 1789319011
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><em>what</em> computation?</p>",
        "id": 623889339,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1789319058
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Kernel-side computation..  reduction/normalisation, definitional equality.. that sort of work the kernel does while checking terms</p>",
        "id": 623889847,
        "sender_full_name": "Heath Sanchez ☉",
        "timestamp": 1789319343
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>So, what I said about optimising the proof so that it typechecks faster?</p>",
        "id": 623889914,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1789319387
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Almost..  same proof, faster checking.You optimise the kernel computation/implementation, not the proof term itself.. the extra proof certifies that optimisation is correct</p>",
        "id": 623890060,
        "sender_full_name": "Heath Sanchez ☉",
        "timestamp": 1789319483
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>How can you optimise the kernel computation without modifying the kernel or modifying the proof?</p>",
        "id": 623890107,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1789319519
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>But probably enough SAIR in the Kernel Arena thread <span aria-label=\"smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f604\" role=\"img\" title=\"smile\">:smile:</span> I’ll let Joachim correct the details</p>",
        "id": 623890108,
        "sender_full_name": "Heath Sanchez ☉",
        "timestamp": 1789319519
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, some higher deity can move the thread probably.</p>",
        "id": 623890176,
        "sender_full_name": "Jeremy Chen",
        "timestamp": 1789319566
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I meant modifying the implementation of the kernel computation, not the input proof. SAIR comps can be  a bit “thinking on their feet”  and yes the page details are vague so I’ll let Joachim pin down the exact rules</p>",
        "id": 623890520,
        "sender_full_name": "Heath Sanchez ☉",
        "timestamp": 1789319814
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>13 messages were moved here from <a class=\"stream-topic\" data-stream-id=\"113488\" href=\"/#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/Lean.20Kernel.20Arena/with/623888064\">#general &gt; Lean Kernel Arena</a> by <span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"687698\">Chris Henson</span>.</p>",
        "id": 623891505,
        "sender_full_name": "Notification Bot",
        "timestamp": 1789320529
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"674484\">Jeremy Chen</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113488-general/topic/SAIR.20Lean.20Kernel.20Challenge/near/623890176\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yes, some higher deity can move the thread probably.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'm no higher deity, but hopefully my moving the relevant messages here is sufficient. </p>\n<p>My understanding is that this is also about picking alternative (proven equivalent) definitions that have more efficient kernel reduction. Like the sort of thing where we have some calculation that may be expensive, but if you find an equivalent statement about naturals, this is efficiently computed.</p>",
        "id": 623892597,
        "sender_full_name": "Chris Henson",
        "timestamp": 1789321157
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For example by writing code like</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">denote</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Ring</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Context</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Expr</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">rec</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">denoteInt</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">NatCast</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">natCast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IntCast</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">intCast</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">denote</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ctx</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₁</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih₂</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ih</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">^</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">e</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>(from <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.lean#L67-L78\">https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Init/Grind/Ring/CommSolver.lean#L67-L78</a>)  instead of just using a recursive <code>def</code> so that the kernel, in <code>whnf</code>, has much fewer piontless things to do.</p>",
        "id": 623903813,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1789327923
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ah ok, same semantics, better computational shape, less kernel work - that clicks</p>",
        "id": 623905852,
        "sender_full_name": "Heath Sanchez ☉",
        "timestamp": 1789329258
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For that competition, it can also be same semantics, better algorithm. Square-and-multiply instead of just iterative multiplying for example. So you win either via better kernel-friendly code or via better math.</p>",
        "id": 623916525,
        "sender_full_name": "Joachim Breitner",
        "timestamp": 1789336432
    }
]